-- The labelled dataset. 46 applications, each with the decision a human
-- actually wants, which is not always the decision the current thresholds
-- produce.
--
-- Read that sentence again, because it is the whole reason this file exists.
-- If the labels were generated by running the rules, the eval would score
-- 100% every time, would stay at 100% through any change, and would be a
-- workflow that prints a number rather than a test. Every label here is a
-- judgement, and the seven rows marked DISAGREES are ones where the judgement
-- and the rules differ on purpose.
--
-- Those seven are what the accuracy number is measuring. The score is not
-- meant to reach 1.0 -- a rule set that agrees with a human on every edge
-- case does not exist, and chasing it produces thresholds overfitted to 46
-- rows. It is meant to move in the right direction when you change a
-- threshold, and to tell you what you broke when it does not.
--
--   psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f n8n/sql/02-golden-set.sql
--
-- Re-runnable: ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE, so fixing a label is editing this file
-- and running it again rather than a hand-written UPDATE nobody records.

